From a58fc9295bd797d0924b982ab44179131e930960 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:38:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] services: network access, Recommended or as in LibreELEC,
 chosen once

LibreELEC Hades changed four of LibreELEC's defaults for what the home
network can reach: file sharing (Samba) is off until turned on and asks
for a password, SSH takes only keys while root has the default password,
the firewall is on for a home network, and AirPlay is off. They are kept
as the defaults, but a person who wants LibreELEC's own behaviour had to
find and change four settings in three places, and nothing said which
way the system was.

Services > "Network access" and a page of the first-start wizard, right
before the one of Samba and SSH, offer one choice: "Recommended (safer)",
Hades' defaults, selected; or "As in LibreELEC": Samba on without a
password, SSH taking root's default password (the file
/storage/.cache/hades-network says libreelec, which sshd-default-password
reads), no firewall, AirPlay on. Choosing As in LibreELEC shows exactly
what will change, with the help that says what it exposes, and asks with
"no" preselected; Recommended changes what differs and shows it (and the
password that samba-config makes where LibreELEC's open share or its
well-known password were in use). Each setting stays its own afterwards;
the choice is read from the settings themselves, so a setting changed by
itself shows "Your own settings". Nothing changes without the person: a
system that is updated keeps every setting, and the wizard runs only on
a first start. The internal disks are not part of it: they stay hidden
the same way with both choices. kodi.log says the network access at each
start and each change (samba, ssh, firewall, airplay).

hades_netaccess.py holds what each choice is made of and what holds, with
nothing of Kodi; netaccess.py is the page of the wizard.

Tested on the host (tools/regress/boot, stage servicessettings) with
stand-ins for Kodi; with this patch reversed it fails. Not run in Kodi.
